digraph account_payable_process_67 {
	graph [rankdir=LR]
	START_NODE [label="" shape=circle width=0.3]
	subgraph CLUSTER_0 {
		"file a copy for internal records" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" [shape=box]
		"file a copy for internal records" -> "create a receiving report"
		"confirm all documents have been amended" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" -> "confirm all documents have been amended"
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_EZTR" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"confirm all documents have been amended" -> "AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_EZTR"
		"create voucher for the documents" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_EZTR" -> "create voucher for the documents"
		"check dates to avoid penalty charges" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--4. Payment_EZTR" -> "check dates to avoid penalty charges"
		"AND_JOIN--4. Payment_EZTR" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"create voucher for the documents" -> "AND_JOIN--4. Payment_EZTR"
		"check dates to avoid penalty charges" -> "AND_JOIN--4. Payment_EZTR"
	}
	START_NODE -> "file a copy for internal records"
	END_NODE [label="" shape=doublecircle width=0.2]
	"AND_JOIN--4. Payment_EZTR" -> END_NODE
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following description is about the account payable process. It starts with filing a copy for internal records. 
After filing a copy for internal records, creating a receiving report should be done. 
When creating a receiving report is completed, you need to confirm all documents have been amended.
Once confirming all documents have been amended occurs, the process is split into 2 parallel branches: creating voucher for the documents and checking dates to avoid penalty charges. 
The process is now completed. 
"
}
